WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.799
Speaker 1: Donald Trump and Rudy Giuliani
are accused of plotting to sell presidential

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:13.130
pardons as Trump's time in the Oval Office
was winding down for the very affordable price,

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:20.720
quite frankly, in context of $2 million apiece,
a former staffer says in a lawsuit.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:27.539
We've already discussed the outrageous sexual
assault allegations that are part of this

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:32.189
lawsuit from former Giuliani staffer Noelle
Dunphy earlier in the show.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:35.820
I now want to focus in on the presidential
pardon part.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.140
There's a Businessinsider article that summarizes
this quite well.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.470
On Monday, Rudy Giuliani was hit with a bombshell
rape civil lawsuit filed by a former staffer.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.940
The staffer alleged in the lawsuit that Giuliani
asked if she knew anyone who wanted to buy

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.640
a presidential pardon.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.520
The suit says Giuliani said he was telling
them selling them for $2 million, splitting

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.400
the profit with Donald Trump.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.630
Now, where do you even start with this?

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:12.170
We have said many times over the last months
an allegation is made against Donald Trump

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.710
and it's written off as obviously not believable.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:19.650
And then another allegation is made that is
very similar and another one and there are

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:23.590
records and lordy, there are tapes or whatever
the case may be.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:28.880
There are already preexisting allegations
that there were all sorts of different ways

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:35.430
that potential pardons were being shopped
and representatives were bringing them to

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.430
Trump.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:40.810
And there were rumors of what about some kind
of financial aspect to this?

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:45.399
And now there is a lawsuit which says under
penalty of perjury, that there was a plan

00:01:45.399 --> 00:01:51.159
between Giuliani and Trump to sell pardons
for $2 million apiece and to split the money.

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:54.200
Is this proof that that was taking place?

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.200
No.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.039
Is this proof that they did it and sold any
pardons?

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:07.280
It is not proof, but it is, again, corroboration
of a pattern that has been alleged from sources

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.140
who have no interaction with each other and
don't know each other.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:14.180
Now, one of the most important questions to
ask here and it's a fair question and it's

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.880
a question that we should ask.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:21.450
Is it explicitly illegal for the president
of the United States to sell pardons?

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.920
The reason we have to ask this question is
one of the things we learned during the Trump

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:32.330
presidency is that just because there are
things that Trump did or is accused of doing

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:38.770
that no former president tried to do, that
is not a guarantee that the thing Trump tried

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.100
to do is actually against the law.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:45.489
And to some degree, one of the things that
Donald Trump exposed through his presidency

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:50.099
is that the checks and balances and separation
of powers that the founders of the Constitution

00:02:50.099 --> 00:02:51.440
put in place.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:56.390
Never expected or assumed that there would
be someone in power like Trump who might try

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.440
to circumvent them.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.239
But let's get to the question.

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:03.140
Is it explicitly illegal for a president to
sell pardons?

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.920
My research is that it is not explicitly illegal.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:12.170
There is not an explicit provision that says
a president can't sell pardons or can't receive

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.070
benefits in exchange for pardons.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:20.680
Benefits could be all sorts of different things,
however, and this is where so many of these

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.420
issues get complicated.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.549
There are legal experts that have said, even
without an explicit provision saying you can't

00:03:27.549 --> 00:03:32.709
sell a pardon as president, you could indeed
as a president selling pardons, be violating

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:34.580
other federal laws, bribery.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.580
You just because you're the president and
you're not explicitly barred from selling

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:45.040
pardons doesn't mean you couldn't be charged
with bribery in accepting money for a pardon.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.340
Fraud, Obstruction of justice.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.750
Obstruction of justice is an interesting one.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:54.170
Imagine that the president sells a pardon
to someone who's under investigation or under

00:03:54.170 --> 00:04:01.030
prosecution by the Justice Department by pardoning
them, potentially preemptively.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:05.760
You are effectively interfering with the administration
of justice because you're saying whatever

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.480
the facts point to, whatever the Justice Department
Justice Department thinks they have based

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.500
on the facts and the evidence.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.739
I'm issuing a preemptive pardon.

00:04:14.739 --> 00:04:18.370
You're interfering with the administration
of justice, and thus it could be an abuse

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.979
of power or obstruction of justice.

00:04:20.979 --> 00:04:28.400
That all being said, those are not explicit
provisions that make it illegal for the president

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.139
of the United States to sell a pardon.

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:37.020
And this is we learned this time and time
again with Trump, we don't actually have strong

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:42.380
enough checks and balances many of us might
have assumed for a long time no one like Trump

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.740
will ever come to power.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.420
So we don't need to worry about some of these
checks and balances that aren't strong enough.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.600
Well, we very quickly learned that we do need
to worry about it.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.220
We will see where this goes.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.800
Stunning blockbuster stuff

